  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>We need to find the number of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math>&nbsp;digit numbers greater than&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>40000</mn></math>&nbsp;and divisible by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math>.</p><p>Case I : Numbers&nbsp;start with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math>.</p><p>Here if the number starts with&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math>&nbsp;it should end with&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;to be divisible by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math>.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/07bd479b-a542-4264-ac04-51f8fcf40369.png\" style=\"width: 380px; height: 77px;\" /></p><p>Case II : Number starts with&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn></math>&nbsp;and the last digit can have&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;or&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math>.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/299d2694-a7da-4eed-9e94-4d95394b61b4.png\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 78px;\" /></p><p>Case III : The number starts with&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn></math>&nbsp;and the last digit should have&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;or&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math>.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/f36ffd05-fe48-445a-9b3a-9cc9fcddef14.png\" style=\"width: 210px; height: 80px;\" /></p><p>Total numbers <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>120</mn></math>.</p><p>Hence this is the correct option.</p>",
